Checking StyleBro's rules, xunit.analyzers' assertion rules where they are warnings or errors and the built-in rules init and migrate turn on (163 ids), changing nothing; --all checks every analyzer's and compiler fix too.
Leaving alone: src/CommonServiceLocator.NinjectAdapter/, src/CommonServiceLocator.NinjectAdapter.Tests/, src/Ninject.Benchmarks/, src/Ninject.Tests/, src/Ninject.Tests.TestAssembly/, src/Ninject.Tests.TestModule/, src/RemotingServer/, src/RemotingTestClient/: StyleCop didn't run there, so the migration set nothing up there (the stylebro-migrate block in .editorconfig names them).
Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net46, net462, net6.0, netstandard2.0).
